== 1. little group, projective representation, irreps
[PASS] all 24 proper rotations fix +k* and -k* (R^T k + pi*lam = k mod 2pi): little group = O
[PASS] rho(g)=U_R (12x12, real orthogonal) composes up to a sign, with both signs occurring: a genuinely projective rep; {+-U_R} is a 48-element group
[PASS] {+-U_R} has 13 involutions: it is GL(2,3), the non-split double cover of O isoclinic to 2O (O x Z2 would have 19); relifting odd elements g -> i g gives a group with 1 involution, i.e. 2O. Relifting rescales odd-element operators by i, which changes no conjugation, no Schur statement and no chi_A2 relation, so the 2O irrep names apply
[PASS] D+ and D- (the B26-build doublets {H_on=2, Lambda=-+2sqrt2}) are rho-invariant
[PASS] D+ and D- irreducible and inequivalent (<chi,chi> = 1.000, 1.000; <chi+,chi-> = 2.4e-17)
[PASS] A2 (x) D+ = D-: chi_{D-}(g) = chi_A2(g) chi_{D+}(g) for all 24 lifts (lift-sign independent), i.e. A2 (x) E1/2 = E5/2
[PASS] 8-dim complement: <chi,chi> = 4.000, no D+ or D- content (overlap 7.6e-17), full commutant dim = 6 = 1+1+4; with projective irreps of dims 2,2,4 only, complement = 2 x G3/2, so D+ and D- have multiplicity 1
== 2. Wigner-Eckart: T1 triples on End(D)
[PASS] D+: the T1-triple space in End(D) is 1-dim; normalised it is a Hermitian, traceless Pauli triple tau_i tau_j = delta_ij + i eps_ijk tau_k (A1/tilt part forced to 0)
[PASS] D-: the T1-triple space in End(D) is 1-dim; normalised it is a Hermitian, traceless Pauli triple tau_i tau_j = delta_ij + i eps_ijk tau_k (A1/tilt part forced to 0)
[PASS] Hom(D+,D-) contains no T1 (dim 0) [so no first-order D+<->D- mixing for an A1 word], and one T1(x)A2 = T2 (dim 1)
[PASS] End(D+) contains no T2 (dim 0) [consistent: an A2 letter's derivative leaves D+ entirely]
